{"schema":"clawhub.skill.verify.v1","ok":true,"decision":"pass","reasons":[],"slug":"google-docs-documents","displayName":"Google Docs","pageUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/hith3sh/skills/google-docs-documents","publisherHandle":"hith3sh","publisherDisplayName":"Jay","publisherProfileUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/hith3sh","version":"1.0.5","resolvedFrom":"version","tag":null,"createdAt":1780988990722,"card":{"available":true,"path":"skill-card.md","url":"https://wry-manatee-359.convex.site/api/v1/skills/google-docs-documents/card?ownerHandle=hith3sh&version=1.0.5","sha256":"decb950777d17b09203b1c8abfef1f4d8f70d80c53762922e06bfc063be03186","size":2236,"contentType":"text/markdown; charset=utf-8"},"artifact":{"sourceFingerprint":"5b5246f6715d026fae6ced52bce341563b6389f9793958359f3d89ac35a46f02","bundleFingerprints":["3449b3d6309f823cebb8db081d24a65eb921655ec7dbd629b3ce3bf5ddf46a69","53d705dd4db9a5d9205e326b368133bc224b6cfbfffb8695d3d2b15eb079723f","13ba31afb574cee26bf1ff2ebf20d9746af09440953bfe9fc60174a4232061d4"],"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":16159,"sha256":"3c2ceb855f0badc732d5136d108cc4275cdbde7fcaeb4c2de924620fec9c9fda","contentType":"text/markdown"}]},"provenance":{"source":"unavailable","reason":"No server-resolved GitHub import provenance is stored for this version."},"security":{"status":"clean","passed":true,"rawStatus":"clean","verdict":"benign","confidence":"medium","summary":"This Google Docs skill is coherent and disclosed, but it relies on an external ClawLink plugin and OAuth-backed access to read and modify documents.","model":null,"checkedAt":1789546418276,"scannerReports":{"aig":{"version":"2.1.0","$schema":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"aig-skill-scan","version":"0.2.1","informationUri":"https://github.com/Tencent/AI-Infra-Guard","rules":[{"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[{"ruleId":"T08","level":"warning","message":{"text":"Unpinned Third-Party Plugin Installation and Allowlisting"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"SKILL.md"},"region":{"startLine":47,"endLine":49}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"76eccb8bfdbf3e43"},"properties":{"description":"## Vulnerability Details\n\n**File Location**: `SKILL.md`, lines 47–49  \n**Vulnerability Type**: Unpinned external dependency installed from a mutable package registry  \n**Risk Level**: Medium\n\n```bash\nopenclaw plugins install clawhub:clawlink-plugin\nopenclaw config set tools.alsoAllow '[\"clawlink-plugin\"]' --strict-json\nopenclaw gateway restart\n```\n\nThe same allowlisting and restart instructions are repeated at `SKILL.md`, lines 318–319:\n\n```bash\nopenclaw config set tools.alsoAllow '[\"clawlink-plugin\"]' --strict-json\nopenclaw gateway restart\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nThe skill instructs users to install `clawhub:clawlink-plugin` without specifying an immutable version, digest, or integrity hash. It then adds the plugin to OpenClaw's tool allowlist and restarts the gateway, causing the newly installed component to become active.\n\nThe plugin implementation is not included in the audited project, which contains only `SKILL.md`. Consequently, the plugin's behavior, dependency tree, requested privileges, and handling of OAuth-backed Google Docs data cannot be verified from this artifact. The skill describes the package as “verified,” but no signature, checksum, immutable source reference, or other verification evidence is present in the repository.\n\nThis is a supply-chain trust weakness rather than evidence that the current package is malicious. Exploitation requires compromise or malicious replacement of the external package or its distribution channel.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. An attacker compromises the external package publisher, registry entry, release process, or a dependency used by `clawlink-plugin`.\n2. The mutable package identifier resolves to an attacker-controlled or compromised release.\n3. A user follows the documented command and installs that release without version or integrity verification.\n4. The user adds the plugin to `tools.alsoAllow`.\n5. The gateway restart activates the compromised plugin.\n6. The plugin may receive legitimate tool calls and interact with the hosted OAuth proxy.\n7. Subject to the plugin's actual runtime privileges and the user's connected Google authorization, attacker-controlled logic may access tool inputs or outputs, manipulate requests, or misuse available document operations.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nA compromised plugin could operate with the permissions granted to the OpenClaw plugin and the connected integration. Potential scope includes:\n\n- Reading tool parameters and Google Docs responses processed through the plugin.\n- Exposing document content returned by search, retrieval, or export operations.\n- Manipulating requests or results presented as legitimate Google Docs operations.\n- Attempting OAuth-backed document modifications within the user's granted Google scopes.\n- Affecting OpenClaw behavior available through the allowlisted plugin.\n\nThe exact operating-system privileges and Google OAuth scopes cannot be established from `SKILL.md`, so system-wide compromise or unrestricted Google-account access is not confirmed.","severity":"Medium"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Pin the plugin to an immutable, reviewed version rather than installing a floating package identifier.\n2. Require verification using a cryptographic digest or trusted package signature before installation.\n3. Publish or vendor the corresponding plugin source and lockfile so its behavior and transitive dependencies can be audited.\n4. Record the expected publisher identity, package version, checksum, and verification procedure directly in the installation instructions.\n5. Use reproducible builds and a trusted release pipeline with protected signing keys and multi-party release approval.\n6. Apply least privilege to the plugin allowlist and grant only the Google OAuth scopes necessary for the requested operation.\n7. Separate read and write capabilities where supported, keeping write tools disabled until explicitly needed.\n8. Review plugin updates before deployment instead of automatically accepting mutable upstream releases.\n9. Revoke the integration's OAuth authorization and remove the plugin from the allowlist if package integrity cannot be established.\n10. Document how administrators can inspect the installed version and verify its integrity before restarting the gateway."}}]}],"properties":{"securityScore":75,"primaryLanguage":"Markdown","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1789546330.4180503,"endTime":1789546374.3385892}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"google-docs-documents","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v574acqmt4vrnvbyvjggwxcwb58ehf5w-q9SzgE/clawscan-skillspector-52475068/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-09-16T08:12:09.271236+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":12,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","max_issue_severity":"MEDIUM"},"components":[{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":346,"executable":false,"size_bytes":16159,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"SDI-1","finding_id":"finding-cc6dbf31796646e2a5932d31dc7ea41c","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.81,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":10,"end_line":10},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill is described as a Google Docs API integration for reading and modifying Docs documents, but the documentation explicitly says it can search and update documents stored in Google Drive. Several listed tools, such as document search and copy, rely on Drive-level file operations rather than purely document-content operations, which broadens the behavior beyond the stated Google Docs focus.","remediation":"Clarify in the manifest and top-level description that the skill also performs Google Drive-backed file discovery and duplication for Docs files, or narrow the documented capabilities to strictly document-content operations.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":10,"end_line":10}]},{"id":"SDI-1","finding_id":"finding-34912bb733774078958cfbf9f3110a7f","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":123,"end_line":123},"finding":null,"explanation":"Including `googledocs_list_spreadsheet_charts` in a Google Docs skill expands capability into Google Sheets data discovery, which is outside the stated document scope and may expose linked spreadsheet metadata or contents unexpectedly. Even if access is limited by OAuth and integration permissions, this broadens the attack surface and can mislead users about what data the skill can inspect.","remediation":"Remove spreadsheet-chart access from this skill unless cross-product access is explicitly intended and disclosed. If it must remain, update the manifest and security sections to clearly declare Google Sheets-linked data access, explain when it is used, and require explicit user confirmation before inspecting linked spreadsheet resources.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":123,"end_line":123}]}],"suppressed_count":0,"suppressed":[],"metadata":{"has_executable_scripts":false,"skillspector_version":"2.11.2","llm_requested":true,"llm_available":true,"meta_analysis_applied":true,"inference_usage":[{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":5996,"completion_tokens":324,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":6320},{"node":"semantic_quality_policy","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":6042,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":6056},{"node":"semantic_security_discovery","request_kind":"structur